{"title":"Career Roadmap · Museum Designer","role":"Museum Designer","summary":"A Museum Designer creates and coordinates the physical environments through which visitors experience collections, exhibitions, cultural narratives, and heritage.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Heritage Conservation Architecture"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Museum Designer creates and coordinates the physical environments through which visitors experience collections, exhibitions, cultural narratives, and heritage."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Architecture","Heritage Conservation","Exhibition Design","Interior Design","Museum Technology","Visitor Experience"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A Museum Designer may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Permanent exhibitions"},{"text":"Temporary exhibitions"},{"text":"Museum galleries"},{"text":"Heritage museums"},{"text":"Archaeological museums"},{"text":"Science and technology museums"},{"text":"Art museums"},{"text":"Cultural centres"},{"text":"Memorials"},{"text":"Interpretation centres"},{"text":"Historic-house museums"},{"text":"Visitor centres"},{"text":"Archives and collection facilities"},{"text":"Museum renovations and adaptive reuse"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The professional must balance heritage authenticity, conservation requirements, storytelling, accessibility, visitor circulation, lighting, environmental control, security, technology, and constructability."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Arch + Foundation"},{"text":"Heritage, conservation, exhibition and interior design"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Museum / Exhibition Designer"},{"text":"Gallery design, interpretation, documenta